<div class="wrap">
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">Life Saving Victoria · First Aid Reporting · 2025/26 Season</div>
    <h1>A branching first aid form, one season in: the data case for the upgrade</h1>
    <p class="lede">In November 2025 a flat first aid form was replaced with a conditional form that presents question sets based on the case. Six seasons of raw records (7,406 cases) were re-analysed from source. Every figure on this page is re-derived from the raw season sheets.</p>

    <div class="tiles">
      <div class="tile"><div class="v">87.1%</div><div class="l">of cases documented within one hour of treatment</div><div class="d">Not measurable under the old form</div></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="v">~4 min</div><div class="l">median time from opening a form to its final edit</div><div class="d">95.0% of forms reach completed status</div></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="v">96.6&ndash;100%</div><div class="l">answer rate on conditional question sets when presented</div><div class="d">Across all six clinical branches</div></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="v">14.0%</div><div class="l">of patients unidentified, down from 27.9% last season</div><div class="d">Unidentified patients halved</div></div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="kicker">Adoption and volume</div>
    <h2>A clean cutover inside a record-scale operation</h2>
    <p class="note">The last old-format form was lodged on 9 November 2025 and the first new-format form on 12 November 2025, with no parallel running. Presentations handled have grown 126 per cent across six seasons. The 2024/25 export spans every calendar month; on the matched November-to-June window the 2025/26 season is 3.6 per cent above 2024/25 (1,518 against 1,465).</p>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>First aid cases per season</h3>
      <p class="sub">2025/26 = 1,494 new form + 24 old form lodged before cutover</p>
      <div class="cols">
