  <section class="sec">
    <div class="kicker">For the conference</div>
    <h2>Ten numbers that carry the story</h2>
    <ol class="wow">
      <li><strong>A three-day cutover.</strong> Last old form 9 November, first new form 12 November; 1,494 new-form cases in season one with no parallel running.</li>
      <li><strong>A richer form did not slow anyone down.</strong> Median 4 minutes from opening to final edit; 95.0 per cent completion.</li>
      <li><strong>87.1 per cent of cases documented within one hour of treatment</strong>, a number that could not be measured before this season.</li>
      <li><strong>Conditional questions are answered 96.6 to 100 per cent</strong> of the time they are presented.</li>
      <li><strong>Unidentified patients halved</strong>, from 27.9 to 14.0 per cent.</li>
      <li><strong>Every resuscitation now carries a clinical timeline</strong>: 11 of 12 detail fields on 7 of 7 cases, against any detail on half of comparable old-form cases.</li>
      <li><strong>Vial-level analgesia auditability</strong>: mean pain 7.1 falling 2.6 points within four minutes across recorded methoxyflurane cases.</li>
      <li><strong>The form now surfaces responder welfare</strong>: 7 peer-support requests in season one that previously had no channel.</li>
      <li><strong>Form improvement is now empirical</strong>: free-text overflow rates name the exact option lists to fix.</li>
      <li><strong>All of this at 126 per cent six-season volume growth</strong>, with January alone carrying 43.6 per cent of the season.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="kicker">Limitations</div>
    <h2>What this data cannot support</h2>
    <ul class="limits">
      <li>The workbook contains no user-satisfaction survey; satisfaction evidence is behavioural (completion rate, speed, adoption, branch answer rates).</li>
      <li>Resuscitation (7) and methoxyflurane (14) counts are small and are reported as counts, not precise rates.</li>
      <li>Old and new taxonomies differ; cross-form trend comparisons use shared categories only.</li>
      <li>Timestamps measure documentation behaviour, not care delivery; the completion long tail includes administrative reopens (incident linking, reclassification).</li>
      <li>Season-on-season volume comparisons use a matched November-to-June window because the 2024/25 export spans all months.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

